**What I created**

| Step | What was made | Key details |
|------|---------------|--------------|
| 1 | 3 model‑space layers | `align_MAIN` (centerline), `rd_EP` (pavement edges), `rd_ES` (shoulder outer edges) |
| 2 | Alignment “ELM‑AVE” | Begins at **E 1000, N 3000** (station 10+00) with 5 legs: S 80° E 800 ft • 40 L curve (500 ft radius) • S 40° W 700 ft • 25 R curve (700 ft radius) • S 65° E 600 ft |
| 3 | Pavement‑edge offsets | 11 ft left/right, drawn on `rd_EP` |
| 4 | Shoulder‑edge offsets | 16 ft left/right (11 ft lanes + 5 ft shoulder), drawn on `rd_ES` |
| 5 | Station labels | Every 100 ft on the alignment (ticks + labels) |
| 6 | Sheet “C‑101” | ANSI D, standard title‑block template |
| 7 | Title‑block fields | `project` = “ELM AVE”, `sheet_title` = “ROADWAY PLAN”, `scale` = “1\"=100'” |
| 8 | Viewport on C‑101 | 1″ = 100′, shows the entire alignment plus shoulders |
| 9 | Entire drawing saved automatically after each call |

**Tool calls (in order)**  

```json
{"name":"align_MAIN","color":"black","linetype":"continuous","lineweight_mm":0.35,"description":"Centerline"} 
{"name":"rd_EP","color":"blue","linetype":"continuous","lineweight_mm":0.25,"description":"Pavement edges"} 
{"name":"rd_ES","color":"red","linetype":"continuous","lineweight_mm":0.25,"description":"Shoulder edges"} 
{"name":"ELM-AVE","begin_station":"10+00","description":"Elm Ave alignment","start":[1000,3000],"legs":[{"bearing":"S 80°00'00\" E","distance":800},{"deflection":"40 L","radius":500,"distance":349.05},{"bearing":"S 40°00'00\" W","distance":700},{"deflection":"25 R","radius":700,"distance":305.43},{"bearing":"S 65°00'00\" E","distance":600}]} 
{"alignment":"ELM-AVE","offsets":[-11,11],"layer":"rd_EP","replace":true} 
{"alignment":"ELM-AVE","offsets":[-16,16],"layer":"rd_ES","replace":true} 
{"alignment":"ELM-AVE","interval":100,"label_offset":6} 
{"name":"C-101","size":"ANSI_D","title_block_fields":{"sheet_title":"ROADWAY PLAN","project":"ELM AVE"},"title_block_template":"standard"} 
{"sheet":"C-101","fields":{"sheet_number":"C-101","project":"ELM AVE","sheet_title":"ROADWAY PLAN","scale":"1\"=100'"} } 
{"sheet":"C-101","center_paper":[15.375,11.375],"width_in":28.0,"height_in":18.0,"model_center":[2138.0,2340.5],"feet_per_inch":100.0,"rotation_deg":0.0}
``` 

**Issues / work‑arounds**

- No errors or confusing messages were returned by any call.
- All coordinates and distances were computed manually using trigonometric relationships:  
  * For the 40 ° left curve (500 ft radius): arc length = 500 × (40 × π/180) ≈ 349.05 ft.  
  * For the 25 ° right curve (700 ft radius): arc length = 700 × (25 × π/180) ≈ 305.43 ft.  
  * The orientation of each straight leg was converted to a quadrant bearing the same way the displacement vector was computed.  
- The viewport center was calculated as the average of the estimated alignment extents (E ≈ 2138 ft, N ≈ 2340 ft) and scaled to the 1″ = 100′ viewport, giving a comfortable margin for the shoulders.  

All drawing tasks are now finished; the alignment, offsets, station labels, sheet and viewport are fully defined in the current document.
